from deepkit import DEEP
M="maths"
DEEP(9,M,"mensuration","cylinder-cone-and-sphere","Surface Area and Volume of Cylinder, Cone and Sphere",
 "A water tank is a cylinder, an ice-cream cone is a cone, and a football is a sphere. To paint the tank or fill the cone we need surface area and volume formulas.",
 ["Surface area is the area of the outside of a solid and is measured in square units. Volume is the space inside and is measured in cubic units. We use π = 22/7 unless told otherwise.",
  "For a cylinder of radius r and height h the curved surface area is 2πrh, the total surface area is 2πr(r + h) and the volume is πr²h.",
  "For a cone of radius r, height h and slant height l, we have l² = r² + h². The curved surface area is πrl, the total surface area is πr(l + r) and the volume is one third of πr²h.",
  "For a sphere of radius r, the surface area is 4πr² and the volume is four thirds of πr³. A hemisphere has curved surface area 2πr², total surface area 3πr² and volume two thirds of πr³."],
 ["curved surface area","total surface area","slant height","volume"],
 ("Find the volume of a cylinder of radius 7 cm and height 10 cm. Use π = 22/7.",["Write the formula: V = πr²h.","Substitute: V = (22/7) × 7 × 7 × 10.","Simplify: (22/7) × 49 = 154, so V = 154 × 10 = 1540.","The volume is 1540 cubic centimetres."]),
 ("Volume of a cone is πr²h, the same as a cylinder.",["A cone fits inside a cylinder of the same base and height","Three cones of water fill that cylinder","So the cone volume is one third of πr²h"]),
 ["Cylinder: CSA 2πrh and volume πr²h.","Cone: CSA πrl and volume one third of πr²h.","Sphere: area 4πr² and volume four thirds of πr³."],
 ["m|The volume of a cylinder is|πr²h|2πrh|πrl|Base area times height.",
  "m|The curved surface area of a cylinder is|2πrh|πr²h|4πr²|Circumference times height.",
  "m|A cone has r = 3 and h = 4. Its slant height is|5|7|6|l = √(9 + 16) = 5.",
  "t|The surface area of a sphere is 4πr².|T|This is the standard formula.",
  "m|Volume of a cylinder with r = 7 cm and h = 10 cm is (π = 22/7)|1540 cm³|154 cm³|440 cm³|(22/7) × 49 × 10 = 1540.",
  "s|Curved surface area of a sphere of radius 7 cm in cm² (π = 22/7)?|616|4 × 22/7 × 49 = 616."])

DEEP(9,M,"statistics","mean-median-and-mode","Mean, Median and Mode",
 "Priya scored 12, 15, 15, 18 and 20 in five tests. Her teacher wants one number that represents her marks. Three different averages can do this.",
 ["Data are the numbers we collect. The mean is the sum of all values divided by the number of values. For 12, 15, 15, 18, 20 the sum is 80, and 80 ÷ 5 = 16, so the mean is 16.",
  "The median is the middle value when the data are arranged in order. With an odd number of values it is the middle one, here 15. With an even number of values we take the mean of the two middle values.",
  "The mode is the value that occurs most often. Here 15 occurs twice, so the mode is 15. A set can have more than one mode or none.",
  "The range is the largest value minus the smallest. Here 20 − 12 = 8. The mean is affected by very large or very small values, but the median is not, so it suits data with extreme values."],
 ["mean","median","mode","range"],
 ("Find the mean, median and mode of 3, 5, 5, 7, 10.",["Mean = (3 + 5 + 5 + 7 + 10) ÷ 5 = 30 ÷ 5 = 6.","The data are already in order and there are 5 values, so the median is the 3rd value, 5.","5 occurs twice and the others once, so the mode is 5.","Range = 10 − 3 = 7."]),
 ("The median is always equal to the mean.",["Mean uses all values","Median is only the middle value","For 1, 2, 9 the mean is 4 but the median is 2"]),
 ["Mean = sum of values ÷ number of values.","Median is the middle value of ordered data.","Mode is the most frequent value."],
 ["m|The mean of 2, 4, 6 is|4|6|3|12 ÷ 3 = 4.",
  "m|The median of 1, 3, 7, 9, 11 is|7|3|9|The middle value of five ordered numbers.",
  "m|The mode of 2, 3, 3, 4, 5, 3 is|3|2|4|3 occurs three times.",
  "t|The range of 5, 9, 12 is 7.|T|12 − 5 = 7.",
  "m|The median of 2, 4, 6, 8 is|5|4|6|Mean of the two middle values (4 + 6) ÷ 2 = 5.",
  "s|The mean of 10, 20, 30, 40 is|25|100 ÷ 4 = 25."])

DEEP(9,M,"coordinate-geometry","plotting-points-and-quadrants","Plotting Points and Quadrants",
 "A treasure map says go 3 steps east and 2 steps north. A pair of numbers can name any place on a flat sheet. This is the idea of coordinates.",
 ["Two number lines cross at right angles. The horizontal one is the x-axis and the vertical one is the y-axis. They meet at the origin O with coordinates (0, 0).",
  "A point is written as (x, y). The x-coordinate or abscissa tells how far to move along the x-axis. The y-coordinate or ordinate tells how far to move up or down. So (3, 2) is 3 right and 2 up.",
  "The axes divide the plane into four quadrants. Quadrant I has x > 0 and y > 0. Quadrant II has x < 0 and y > 0. Quadrant III has both negative and Quadrant IV has x > 0 and y < 0.",
  "A point on the x-axis has y = 0 and a point on the y-axis has x = 0. The order matters, so (3, 2) and (2, 3) are different points."],
 ["origin","abscissa","ordinate","quadrant"],
 ("In which quadrant does the point (−4, 5) lie? Give the abscissa and ordinate.",["The abscissa is the x-coordinate, which is −4.","The ordinate is the y-coordinate, which is 5.","x is negative and y is positive, so the point is in Quadrant II."]),
 ("(3, 2) and (2, 3) are the same point.",["The first number is always x","(3, 2) is 3 right and 2 up, while (2, 3) is 2 right and 3 up","They are different points"]),
 ["A point is written (x, y).","The axes make four quadrants.","Points on the x-axis have y = 0."],
 ["m|The point (0, 0) is called the|origin|abscissa|quadrant|It is where the axes meet.",
  "m|The point (−2, −3) lies in Quadrant|III|II|IV|Both coordinates are negative.",
  "m|The abscissa of (5, −1) is|5|−1|0|The x-coordinate comes first.",
  "t|A point on the y-axis has x = 0.|T|Every point of the y-axis has abscissa 0.",
  "m|The point (4, −6) lies in Quadrant|IV|I|II|x is positive and y is negative.",
  "s|What is the ordinate of the point (7, 3)?|3;three|The second number is the ordinate."])

DEEP(9,M,"trigonometry","trigonometric-ratios","Trigonometric Ratios of an Acute Angle",
 "A ladder leans against a wall. Its steepness depends on the angle it makes with the ground. Trigonometry gives the steepness as a ratio.",
 ["In a right triangle the side opposite the right angle is the hypotenuse. For an angle θ, the side opposite θ is the opposite side and the other side is the adjacent side.",
  "The three main ratios are sin θ = opposite ÷ hypotenuse, cos θ = adjacent ÷ hypotenuse and tan θ = opposite ÷ adjacent. A memory aid is SOH CAH TOA.",
  "For a 3, 4, 5 right triangle and the angle opposite the side 3 we get sin θ = 3/5, cos θ = 4/5 and tan θ = 3/4. The reciprocals are cosec θ = 1/sin θ, sec θ = 1/cos θ and cot θ = 1/tan θ.",
  "Some values to remember are sin 30° = 1/2, cos 60° = 1/2, sin 45° = cos 45° = 1/√2 and tan 45° = 1. Also sin²θ + cos²θ = 1 for every angle."],
 ["hypotenuse","sine","cosine","tangent"],
 ("In a right triangle, the opposite side is 5 and the hypotenuse is 13. Find the adjacent side, sin θ, cos θ and tan θ.",["Adjacent² = 13² − 5² = 169 − 25 = 144, so the adjacent side is 12.","sin θ = 5/13.","cos θ = 12/13.","tan θ = 5/12."]),
 ("sin θ = adjacent ÷ hypotenuse.",["Sine uses the opposite side","Cosine uses the adjacent side","Remember SOH: sine is opposite over hypotenuse"]),
 ["sin = opposite/hypotenuse, cos = adjacent/hypotenuse, tan = opposite/adjacent.","sin²θ + cos²θ = 1.","tan 45° = 1 and sin 30° = 1/2."],
 ["m|sin θ equals|opposite ÷ hypotenuse|adjacent ÷ hypotenuse|opposite ÷ adjacent|SOH.",
  "m|tan 45° equals|1|0|1/2|Opposite and adjacent are equal.",
  "m|For the 3, 4, 5 triangle, cos θ (angle opposite 3) is|4/5|3/5|3/4|Adjacent 4 over hypotenuse 5.",
  "t|sin²θ + cos²θ = 1.|T|This is the basic identity.",
  "m|sin 30° equals|1/2|1/√2|1|It is a standard value.",
  "s|If sin θ = 3/5, find cos θ as a fraction.|4/5|The missing side is 4."])

DEEP(9,M,"probability","basics-of-probability","Basics of Probability",
 "Before a cricket match the captains toss a coin. Nobody knows the result, yet we can say the chance of heads is one out of two.",
 ["An experiment is an activity with results that we cannot predict, like tossing a coin or rolling a die. Each possible result is an outcome and a group of outcomes is an event.",
  "The probability of an event E is P(E) = number of favourable outcomes ÷ total number of outcomes, when all outcomes are equally likely. For a die, P(getting 4) = 1/6.",
  "Probability is always between 0 and 1. An impossible event has probability 0 and a sure event has probability 1. For example P(getting 7 on a die) = 0.",
  "The probability that an event does not happen is 1 − P(E). If P(rain) = 2/5 then P(no rain) = 3/5. The probabilities of all outcomes add up to 1."],
 ["outcome","event","favourable outcomes","sure event"],
 ("A bag has 3 red and 5 blue balls. One ball is drawn at random. Find P(red) and P(not red).",["Total outcomes = 3 + 5 = 8.","P(red) = 3/8.","P(not red) = 1 − 3/8 = 5/8.","This matches the blue balls, 5 out of 8."]),
 ("The probability of an event can be 3/2.",["Favourable outcomes cannot be more than total outcomes","So the fraction cannot exceed 1","Probability lies between 0 and 1"]),
 ["P(E) = favourable outcomes ÷ total outcomes.","0 ≤ P(E) ≤ 1.","P(not E) = 1 − P(E)."],
 ["m|The probability of getting heads on a fair coin is|1/2|1|1/4|One favourable out of two.",
  "m|A die is rolled. P(an even number) is|1/2|1/3|1/6|Three of six numbers are even.",
  "m|The probability of a sure event is|1|0|1/2|It always happens.",
  "t|A probability can be negative.|F|It is always between 0 and 1.",
  "m|If P(E) = 2/5, then P(not E) is|3/5|2/5|1/5|1 − 2/5 = 3/5.",
  "s|A die is rolled. What is P(getting a number greater than 4)?|1/3|Only 5 and 6 are favourable, 2/6 = 1/3."])
